<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

    {{!-- Content Security Policy.

         Defense-in-depth: even if an XSS vector slips past every
         sanitizer, the browser refuses to execute scripts from
         off-allowlist origins, refuses connect-src to off-allowlist
         hosts, and blocks framing of this page.

         Tradeoffs we accept:
         - 'unsafe-inline' on script-src is REMOVED. Every theme-side
           inline <script> has been externalized (assets/js/boot/*,
           assets/js/page/*, assets/js/reader.js, etc.); template-data
           bindings (MO_API_BASE, mo-digest-assets) are emitted as
           <meta> tags read by tiny bootstrap scripts. If Ghost's
           {{ghost_head}} or admin Code Injection injects inline JS,
           those will be blocked — verify Plausible / analytics still
           load (Plausible's proxied build is an external <script>,
           so it should be fine).
         - 'unsafe-inline' on style-src for inline style="..." attrs
           on Ghost-rendered post bodies + a few theme spots.
         - img-src https: is broad; Ghost feature_images come from
           any admin-configured CDN (HubSpot CDN during migration,
           Ghost CDN after).

         frame-ancestors is HTTP-header-only (not supported in meta).
         Set via Ghost Pro's Cloudflare in front, or accept that
         click-jacking surface is unmitigated for now.

         Pass 2 A05-1, A05-2, A05-3. --}}
    {{!-- connect-src is named-host, not wildcard. `https://*.workers.dev`
         would allow any attacker.workers.dev as a JWT exfiltration
         target (Codex audit 2026-05-11: "MOAuth.fetch sends member
         JWTs to any URL"). The 12 hosts below are exactly the workers
         that BACKEND-INVENTORY.md §6 lists as theme-callable. New
         worker → add it here AND to the MOAuth.fetch allowlist
         harvest in admin-auth.js.

         The Blob host plus the five vercel.app hosts are the read-only
         data sources for The Faith Received corpora — 29,491 works
         across 7 collections (EEBO, Patrologia Latina/Graeca/
         Orientalis, Augustine, the TFR Latin corpus and
         the confessions), together with their scripture, topic and
         reference indexes. See assets/js/faith-corpora.js for the
         registry.

         pangrammata.vercel.app was removed from connect-src 2026-07-28
         when that collection was pulled. Nothing in the theme fetches
         it any more; leaving the host allowed would widen the CSP for
         no reason.

         All are fetched anonymously by faith-corpora.js /
         faith-reader.js / faith-library-browse.js — never via
         MOAuth.fetch, so none carries a member JWT. All serve
         Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *. They belong to the author MO
         is porting from, not to MO; slated to be replaced by an
         MO-owned R2 mirror before public launch. --}}
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://unpkg.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://js.stripe.com https://plausible.io https://mo-admin.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' https:; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.buzzsprout.com https://js.stripe.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://embed.spotify.com https://open.spotify.com https://mereorthodoxy.com https://mo-test.ghost.io; connect-src 'self' https://mo-test.ghost.io https://mo-admin.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-audio.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-bible.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-ebook-access.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-email.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-errors.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-forms.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-gift.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-kit.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-kit-bridge.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-membership.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-pdf.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-podcast-feed.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-search.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-tfr-library.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://0ss8v4l06kodnhp0.public.blob.vercel-storage.com https://mo-tfr.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://eebo-backup.vercel.app https://pld-patrologia-latina.vercel.app https://patrologia-graeca.vercel.app https://patrologia-orientalis.vercel.app https://aquinas-studies.vercel.app https://mereorthodoxy.com https://www.mereorthodoxy.com https://api.stripe.com https://plausible.io https://challenges.cloudflare.com; form-action 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests" />
    <meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" />

    {{!-- Per-template document title + social meta.

         This used to be a flat `<title>{{meta_title}}</title>`, which
         is correct for posts, pages, tags and authors — Ghost resolves
         meta from the record behind the route. It is wrong for the
         ~150 routes.yaml routes bound straight to a template with no
         Ghost Page record: {{meta_title}} falls all the way back to
         the site title, and {{ghost_head}} emits that same site title
         as og:title / twitter:title. Every one of them unfurled as
         "Mere Orthodoxy | Faith, Formation, Church, and Culture" —
         reported 2026-07-29 for /daily-liturgy/read/.

         So the title belongs to the template, not the layout. Each
         one fills {{#contentFor "moHead"}} with its own <title> plus
         og:/twitter: overrides; index/post/page/tag/author/error fill
         it with {{meta_title}}, exactly what was here before.

         The og:/twitter: overrides work because this block sits above
         {{ghost_head}} and every scraper takes the FIRST tag it sees.
         Same first-tag-wins trick as the og:image fallback below.
         Ghost still emits its site-level pair further down; harmless,
         and there is no way to suppress it from a theme.

         TRAP: an empty block emits no <title> at all. `npm run
         check:meta` fails the build if any template using this layout
         is missing its moHead block — do not delete that check. --}}
    {{{block "moHead"}}}
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#1d1b18">

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://js.stripe.com" />
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://plausible.io" />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IM+Fell+Great+Primer:ital@0;1&family=Source+Serif+Pro:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400;1,600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="{{asset "built/screen.min.css"}}" />

    {{!-- No-JS fallback: screen.css hides "Parent > Child" nav items
         pre-JS to prevent the flicker before nav-dropdowns.js rebuilds
         them into dropdowns. If JS doesn't run at all, this <noscript>
         re-shows them so the children stay reachable. --}}
    <noscript>
        <style>
            [data-nav-dropdowns] a[data-nav-label*=">"] { display: inline-flex; }
        </style>
    </noscript>

    {{!-- Membership API base URL. mo-api-base.js (loaded with the
         other boot scripts) reads this and sets window.MO_API_BASE
         for the membership-related JS to consume. Externalizing the
         per-template inline setter lets us drop 'unsafe-inline' from
         the CSP. --}}
    <meta name="mo-api-base" content="{{@custom.membership_api_base}}" />

    {{!-- Ghost's asset hash, for JS that fetches /assets/data/*.json
         directly. Those URLs skip the {{asset}} helper but not Ghost's
         one-year cache header, so a regenerated data file would stay
         invisible until the header expired. mo-asset-version.js reads
         the hash out of this and moAssetUrl() appends it. Any asset
         works — they all carry the same theme-wide stamp. --}}
    <meta name="mo-asset-version" content="{{asset "built/boot.min.js"}}" />

    {{#if @custom.content_api_key}}
    <meta name="ghost-content-api-key" content="{{@custom.content_api_key}}" />
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- New-member Offer for the referral program. referral.js reads
         this to repoint the /membership/ CTA when a visitor arrives via
         a ?ref= link. Empty = single-sided referral (no new-member offer). --}}
    {{#if @custom.referral_offer_url}}
    <meta name="mo-referral-offer" content="{{@custom.referral_offer_url}}" />
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- Trusted destinations for MOAuth.fetch. admin-auth.js reads
         this ONCE at IIFE time (before {{{body}}} renders, before any
         page-template scripts run) and freezes the set. Pipe-separated
         URL list because some values may contain commas or spaces in
         the future; pipe is reliably URL-safe.

         Codex audit 2026-05-11 (P0 finding): the previous
         implementation harvested allowlisted hosts from
         [data-worker-url], [data-kit-bridge-url], [data-api-base]
         elements in the DOM and re-harvested on a miss. An XSS could
         inject <div data-worker-url="https://attacker.example"> and
         then call MOAuth.fetch on attacker.example — the new element
         got harvested on miss, attacker host became trusted, JWT went
         to attacker. Closure-private prevented extraction but
         DOM-injection extended the allowlist.

         Hardcoded here at template render time so the runtime never
         re-reads DOM-mutable state. New worker → add its URL to this
         list AND to the connect-src directive in the CSP above. --}}
    <meta name="mo-trusted-hosts" content="{{@custom.kit_worker_url}}|{{@custom.admin_worker_url}}|{{@custom.search_worker_url}}|{{@custom.error_worker_url}}|{{@custom.podcast_feed_url}}|{{@custom.membership_api_base}}|{{@custom.gift_worker_url}}|{{@custom.kit_bridge_url}}|https://mo-audio.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev|https://mo-pdf.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev|https://mo-forms.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev|https://mo-ebook-access.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev|https://mo-email.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev" />

    {{!-- Cloudflare Turnstile site key. Public-by-design (key is
         visible in the rendered widget anyway). Hardcoded as a meta
         tag rather than a Ghost @custom setting because @custom is
         at the 20-setting cap. site-forms.js reads it on contact +
         submissions pages. Codex audit 2026-05-11 follow-up. --}}
    <meta name="turnstile-site-key" content="0x4AAAAAADNUmqxNMMwe32iy" />

    {{!-- Base URL for the mo-bible Cloudflare Worker (proxies api.bible).
         Hardcoded here rather than via @custom because the setting cap is
         hit. The worker URL is fixed once deployed; change here if the
         worker is ever moved to a custom domain. /bible/ JS reads this
         and prepends to /api/bible/v1/* calls. --}}
    <meta name="mo-bible-base" content="https://mo-bible.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev" />

    {{!-- Turnstile JS. Loads on every page so any future form that
         wants bot protection can render <div class="cf-turnstile">
         without per-template script tags. Async + defer so it doesn't
         block first paint. --}}
    <script src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>

    {{!-- Fallback social-share image. Only emitted when the current
         context has NO feature image of its own, so a page/post with a
         feature image unfurls with that image instead of the house card.
         Routes with no image (home, custom routes.yaml pages without a
         data-bound page) fall back to the house share card instead of
         unfurling blank.
         See SEO-AGENT S6.2 / S6.11. Share card is 1200x630.

         SCOPE TRAP (fixed 2026-07-28): this used to read
         `{{#unless feature_image}}`. In default.hbs the root context is
         the route context, NOT the post object — post.hbs enters it with
         `{{#post}}`, tag.hbs with `{{#tag}}`. So bare `feature_image` was
         always undefined, the unless always passed, and every article
         emitted the house card. Because this block sits ABOVE
         {{ghost_head}} and scrapers take the FIRST og:image, the house
         card beat Ghost's real feature-image tag on every single post.
         Must be `post.feature_image` / `tag.feature_image`.

         This block stays ABOVE {{ghost_head}} on purpose: on imageless
         routes Ghost emits `twitter:card = summary` (small card), and
         first-tag-wins is what keeps those unfurling as
         summary_large_image. --}}
    {{#unless post.feature_image}}
    {{#unless tag.feature_image}}
    {{#unless author.cover_image}}
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{asset "images/mo-share-card.jpg"}}" />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{asset "images/mo-share-card.jpg"}}" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    {{/unless}}
    {{/unless}}
    {{/unless}}

    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Mere Orthodoxy",
      "url": "{{@site.url}}",
      "logo": "{{@site.logo}}",
      "description": "{{@site.description}}",
      "foundingDate": "2005",
      "sameAs": [
        "https://x.com/maborodoxy",
        "https://www.facebook.com/mereorthodoxy",
        "https://www.instagram.com/mereorthodoxy"
      ]
    }
    </script>

    {{ghost_head}}

    {{!-- Plausible tracker: Ghost also injects its own Plausible script
         via ghost_head, but it loads from plausible.io which ad blockers
         intercept. This proxied copy goes through mo-admin, bypassing
         blocklists. data-api tells the script to POST events to our
         proxy instead of plausible.io directly.

         Custom events (e.g. "Article Read" on posts) fire via
         window.plausible(...) on the 'load' event. See post.hbs. --}}
    <script defer
      data-domain="mereorthodoxy.com"
      data-api="{{@custom.admin_worker_url}}/pa/e"
      src="{{@custom.admin_worker_url}}/pa/js"></script>

    {{!-- Preload the logo image so the browser fetches it during
         parsing, before the <img> is discovered in the body. Eliminates
         the visible pop-in when the header paints before the logo
         download completes. --}}
    <link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{asset "images/mere-o-logo.png"}}" />

    <link rel="icon" type="image/jpeg" href="{{asset "images/mere-o-fav-icon.jpg"}}" />
    <link rel="shortcut icon" type="image/jpeg" href="{{asset "images/mere-o-fav-icon.jpg"}}" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{asset "images/mere-o-fav-icon.jpg"}}" />
</head>
<body class="{{body_class}}"
      {{#if @custom.podcast_feed_url}}data-podcast-feed-url="{{@custom.podcast_feed_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @custom.kit_worker_url}}data-kit-worker-url="{{@custom.kit_worker_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @custom.search_worker_url}}data-search-worker-url="{{@custom.search_worker_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @custom.admin_worker_url}}data-admin-worker-url="{{@custom.admin_worker_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @custom.error_worker_url}}data-error-worker-url="{{@custom.error_worker_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @member}}data-member-email="{{@member.email}}" data-member-status="{{@member.status}}"{{/if}}>

    {{!-- Boot bundle: liturgical-class, mo-api-base, mo-asset-version,
         admin-auth, safe-href, safe-redirect, DOMPurify. MUST load
         before {{{body}}} — page templates call window.MOAuth.fetch
         and window.MOSafeHref synchronously on load.

         title-fix.js was dropped 2026-07-29. It patched document.title
         and injected robots noindex from a path map, which never
         reached a link-preview scraper — none of them run JS, which is
         why every custom route still unfurled with the site title.
         Both jobs are now server-rendered in each template's moHead
         block, and the client-side map was actively overwriting the
         better server titles. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "built/boot.min.js"}}"></script>

    <header class="site-header">
        <div class="container header-inner">
            <a href="{{@site.url}}" class="brand" aria-label="Mere Orthodoxy home">
                <img src="{{asset "images/mere-o-logo.png"}}" alt="Mere Orthodoxy" class="brand-logo" width="164" height="72" />
            </a>
            <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary" data-nav-dropdowns>
                {{!-- Use this.url so Handlebars resolves the nav item's
                     `url` property instead of invoking Ghost's {{url}}
                     helper, which was returning "/" for every item.
                     `data-nav-dropdowns` triggers nav-dropdowns.js to
                     regroup flat items into dropdowns using the
                     "Parent > Child" label convention managed in
                     Ghost Admin → Settings → Navigation. --}}
                {{#foreach @site.navigation}}
                    <a href="{{this.url}}" data-nav-label="{{label}}">{{label}}</a>
                {{/foreach}}
            </nav>
            <div class="nav-actions">
                {{!-- Search trigger — opens Ghost's built-in sodo-search
                     modal (auto-loaded by ghost_head). Keyboard "/" also
                     opens it. --}}
                <button class="nav-search" type="button" data-mo-search aria-label="Search articles">
                    <svg class="nav-search-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle>
                        <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line>
                    </svg>
                </button>
                {{#unless @member}}
                    <button class="sign-in" data-portal="signin">Sign in</button>
                    <a href="/membership/" class="btn btn-primary">Become a Member</a>
                {{else}}
                    <button class="sign-out" data-portal="signout">Sign out</button>
                    <a href="/dashboard/" class="btn btn-primary btn-account">{{#if @member.name}}{{@member.name}}{{else}}Dashboard{{/if}}</a>
                {{/unless}}
            </div>
            <button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mobile-nav" aria-label="Open menu">
                <span class="nav-toggle-bar"></span>
                <span class="nav-toggle-bar"></span>
                <span class="nav-toggle-bar"></span>
            </button>
        </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mobile-nav" id="mobile-nav" hidden>
        <div class="mobile-nav-backdrop"></div>
        <aside class="mobile-nav-panel" role="dialog" aria-label="Site navigation">
            <div class="mobile-nav-head">
                <span class="mobile-nav-wordmark"><em>Mere Orthodoxy</em></span>
                <button class="mobile-nav-close" type="button" aria-label="Close menu">&times;</button>
            </div>
            <nav class="mobile-nav-links" aria-label="Primary" data-nav-dropdowns data-nav-mode="mobile">
                {{#foreach @site.navigation}}
                    <a href="{{this.url}}" data-nav-label="{{label}}">{{label}}</a>
                {{/foreach}}
            </nav>
            <div class="mobile-nav-actions">
                <button class="mobile-nav-search" type="button" data-mo-search aria-label="Search articles">
                    <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle>
                        <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line>
                    </svg>
                    <span>Search articles</span>
                </button>
                {{#unless @member}}
                    <button class="mobile-nav-signin" data-portal="signin">Sign in</button>
                    <a href="/membership/" class="btn btn-primary">Become a Member</a>
                {{else}}
                    <a href="/dashboard/" class="btn btn-primary btn-account">{{#if @member.name}}{{@member.name}}{{else}}Dashboard{{/if}}</a>
                    <button class="mobile-nav-signout" data-portal="signout">Sign out</button>
                {{/unless}}
            </div>
        </aside>
    </div>

    {{!-- Nav dropdowns loaded here (after header + mobile-nav are in
         the DOM but before {{{body}}} paints) to prevent the flat-nav
         items from visibly popping into grouped dropdowns. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "js/nav-dropdowns.js"}}"></script>

    {{!-- Header behaviors loaded here (after header + mobile-nav are
         in the DOM but before {{{body}}} paints). The syncOffset()
         function measures the fixed header's height and sets
         body.paddingTop to push page content below it. If this runs
         in the footer bundle, the hero/content renders at top:0
         (under the header) and then jumps down when the footer
         scripts execute — visible as the "everything shifts up then
         back down" pop-in. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "js/boot/header-behaviors.js"}}"></script>

    {{{body}}}

